14,249/19,440 are whole-run CPU? If whole-run CPU: integer total CPU 14,249 over 381 s = 37.4x average whole-run; the 68.5x is window-loop only. Then consistency: CPU_loop = total − CPU_other. Can't fully verify, but the arithmetic closes within ~3% either way. So: the occupancy numbers are consistent with "less work, proportionally shorter loop"; the residual is a few percent, not a 20% scheduling defect. The remaining measurement: thread-state sampler (per plan §5), and a split-stage timer.

