  **`t.mz = cmz`** — the comment at :1020 says "the weighted centroid, as OpenMS reports". But mzEstimator() default is "apex"! OpenMS path reports apex m/z by default (t.mz = mt[findMaxByIntPeak].getMZ()). The integer path reports the CENTROID m/z regardless of the estimator setting. Wait — in splitIntegerTraces, children go through toTrace → c.mz = apex or per estimator. But the pre-split traces' mz=cmz is replaced by toTrace's mz after split. But if ms2_split == 0 (split_valleys off), splitIntegerTraces returns early (in.size()<2? no — split_valleys<=0 → return move(in)) and traces keep mz=cmz — centroid, while OpenMS path with split off would report apex. So with split_valleys=0 the detectors' m/z semantics diverge. Default ms2_split=7.0 so OK by default. Also for MS1 — always OpenMS detector. Minor divergence, worth one line.

  Also `t.rt = rtAxis()[sl.rt_index[fap]]` — APEX RT, while OpenMS reports CENTROID RT (t.rt = mt.getCentroidRT()). After splitting, children go through toTrace which sets centroid RT — consistent. Unsplit path diverges.

  **Charge:min_charge default 2** — validated, fine.

