commit e3c6eb4a81afa732e81c22219249b93608361600
Author: Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 07:08:11 2026 +0200

    Make trace:detector=integer the default, falling back to openms when the vendor calibration is absent
    
    The integer detector is faster and ~40% lighter, and the two detectors agree to about 1% of
    identified peptides in either direction. It needs the vendor flight-time calibration; rather than
    refuse an input without one -- which would make the tool unusable on files it handled before -- it
    warns and falls back to the OpenMS detector. Failing closed is the right answer when the alternative
    is inventing a calibration and emitting wrong masses; it is the wrong answer when a second detector
    needs no calibration at all. The emitted mzML records which one ran as spx:detector.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

