commit 7d6e56f2d8a0e915cfa5bf9a302414909a505c10
Author: Oliver <oliver.kohlbacher@uni-tuebingen.de>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 07:33:42 2026 +0200

    Prep: no per-peak frame map, no membership byte, exact-reserved seed list
    
    A peak's frame is the loop variable at every hot site (one binary search over frame_off at the two
    that lack it), and membership IS inten > noise. The accepted-peak list carries (frame, peak) pairs
    so nothing downstream needs a map. The seed counter measured 100% of above-noise peaks as seeds at
    the shipped snr of 1.0, so the P/4 reserve grew by doubling to ~2P: count first, reserve exactly.
    Prep goes from ~13 B/peak to 4. Output-neutral by construction; digest-gated.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

