  **Section 3 — correctness of span implementation.** Walk through the asked items:
  - Dangling st: stores are never moved after st is set (ms1_store :2704 local, wst :3264 task-local, bst/stores pre-sized vectors). Verified safe. BUT note the pattern is one refactor away from UAF — st is a raw pointer set manually at :2712, :3311, :3326, :3335; nothing enforces it. Also makeSpan returns st unset; an empty MassTrace in toTrace returns a default Trace (st=nullptr) which is only repaired by the caller loops; if any future caller forgets, xv() derefs nullptr. Checked: all three call sites set it.
  - Rebase: band absorb at :3303-3310 and chunk absorb at :1127-1132 rebase off after absorb; joins via implicit taskgroups; offsets are indices. Safe as implemented. One real inconsistency: absorb()'s bins merge assumes every non-empty inten arena has a bins arena; true today (detection always resizes bins at :1017; EPD chunks have empty bins and inten — absorbed after wst.bins freed :1124) but the invariant is uncommented at the absorb site.
